<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       DROIDWORKS_FORMAT_TIERS_1 (packet B1) — the moral consequence of destroying
       a sapient droid's mind: "deformat sapient = murder thought per faction
       ethics" (packet B1; build spec unit 9; droid_system_spec.md section 8).

       Fired by RimMandrake.StarWars.Droidworks.Recipe_DWFormatBase whenever an
       operation takes a droid that WAS sapient below the programmable rung.

       🔑 HOW A WITNESS THOUGHT ACTUALLY REACHES A PAWN IN 1.6. Vanilla has no
       non-ideoligious witness-thought route left: ThoughtUtility's own
       organ-harvest and execution paths do nothing but record a HistoryEvent, and
       the mood memory is granted by a PreceptComp_KnowsMemoryThought on whichever
       ideoligion holds an opinion. So this file ships the two halves the platform
       owns — the event, and the thought a precept can point at — and the precept
       itself is campaign data.

       ⛔ NOT WIRED HERE, AND OWED: no ideoligion in this repo yet reacts to
       RSW_DW_DeformattedSapientDroid, so with Ideology active a deformat currently
       moves faction goodwill but produces no colonist thought. The precept wiring
       belongs with the faction/ideoligion layer (RimUtinni), not with the
       platform. Recipe_DWFormatBase grants RSW_DW_KnowSapientDroidDeformatted
       directly ONLY when Ideology is inactive, so the two routes can never
       double-count.
  ======================================================================== -->
  <HistoryEventDef>
    <defName>RSW_DW_DeformattedSapientDroid</defName>
    <label>destroyed a sapient droid's mind</label>
  </HistoryEventDef>

  <ThoughtDef>
    <defName>RSW_DW_KnowSapientDroidDeformatted</defName>
    <thoughtClass>Thought_Memory</thoughtClass>
    <durationDays>10</durationDays>
    <stackLimit>5</stackLimit>
    <stackedEffectMultiplier>0.75</stackedEffectMultiplier>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>sapient droid deformatted</label>
        <description>Someone here scraped a thinking droid down to bare metal. Whatever it had become is gone. It did not have to be that way.</description>
        <baseMoodEffect>-8</baseMoodEffect>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </ThoughtDef>

</Defs>
